# Scoped for repo-root-context builds (tester-unified, wheel-builder — both built via
# `docker build -f <dir>/Dockerfile ... /workspaces/vbpub`). Whitelist ONLY what they
# COPY (or, for wheel-builder, may COPY in future — today it's stateless), so the
# build context stays tiny — everything else (.git, .worktrees, logs, other stacks) is
# excluded. NOTE: this whitelist means a repo-root `docker build` sees only these
# dirs; other stacks build from their own subdirectory contexts, not here.
*
!ciu
!cmru
!assay
!topos
!nyxloom
!wheel-builder
# Nyxloom's image now builds with the repository root as context. Expose only
# the cli-extended package source that its wheel build copies; keep the rest of
# libraries/ out of unrelated root-context builds.
!libraries
libraries/*
!libraries/cli-extended
libraries/cli-extended/*
!libraries/cli-extended/src
libraries/cli-extended/src/*
!libraries/cli-extended/src/cli_extended
# tester-unified builds cli-extended and cmru OFFLINE from these COPYed sources
# (never from an index; BG-05): the cli-extended build needs its pyproject and
# the README its metadata names; cmru's pyproject packages
# `../libraries/worktree/src` alongside it.
!libraries/cli-extended/pyproject.toml
!libraries/cli-extended/README.md
!libraries/worktree
libraries/worktree/*
!libraries/worktree/src
libraries/worktree/src/*
!libraries/worktree/src/worktree
# tester-unified's requirements generator (the only file of that directory the
# image needs; the parent must be re-included first).
!tester-unified
tester-unified/*
!tester-unified/gen-requirements.py
# scripts/ is otherwise excluded wholesale; whitelist just the one project
# tester-unified installs from (its pyproject is the closure's source of truth).
# The parent directory must be re-included first or the child is never reached.
!scripts
scripts/*
!scripts/cgroup-profiler

# Drop heavy/generated content within the whitelisted projects.
**/.git
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/.mypy_cache
**/node_modules
**/.worktrees
# cgroup-profiler ships a built venv and captured runs; neither belongs in a
# build context (the venv alone is 500 MB).
scripts/cgroup-profiler/venv
scripts/cgroup-profiler/runs
scripts/cgroup-profiler/output
